# Capability review, two releases

Six axes, a fixed order, and a shared 0–5 scale, which is the only arrangement
in which the enclosed areas mean anything. The comparison the shape makes is
that 2.0 gained on accessibility and documentation and gave up nothing.

```mdv radar
title: Platform capability review
category: capability
value: score
series: release
maxValue: 5
gridShape: polygon
fill: true
format: table
---
capability    | release | score
Throughput    | v1.4    |   3.1
Latency       | v1.4    |   3.6
Accessibility | v1.4    |   2.2
Docs          | v1.4    |   2.8
Security      | v1.4    |   3.9
Extensibility | v1.4    |   3.0
Throughput    | v2.0    |   3.4
Latency       | v2.0    |   3.7
Accessibility | v2.0    |   4.4
Docs          | v2.0    |   4.1
Security      | v2.0    |   4.0
Extensibility | v2.0    |   3.5
```
